## Context

The adopted installation is a clone at `~/.agents`, not a repository hidden
inside one runtime's profile and not a second canonical `~/.idh` pointer. The
path is the reference installation location, not an API: tracked code must keep
working when the checkout is cloned elsewhere, moved, or reached through an
installed symlink.

This supersedes 0978 and 0986. Their `~/.claude` to `~/.idh` migration,
projection manifest and quiet-window cutover are historical. Runtime-owned
profiles such as `~/.claude` and `~/.codex` remain runtime state; adapters may
register links or native plugins there, but they do not become alternate names
for the repository.

## Relevant files

- `adapters/lifecycle.py`, `adapters/projections.json` — installation and validation
- `scripts/bashrc-loader.sh`, `scripts/shell-init.sh` — portable shell entry points
- `adapters/codex/hooks.json` — hook resolution through its installed symlink
- `skills/dream/provenance.py`, `skills/dream/read-index.py` — remaining fixed roots
- `README.md`, `STATE.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `docs/idh-install-strategy.md` — installation contract and priorities

## Progress

Planning and documentation landed in PRs #1089/#1090. This parent is now an
integration tracker, not the close claim for PR #1091.

- [x] README, STATE and ROADMAP describe the portable `~/.agents` clone.
- [x] Installation, operations and adapter guides distinguish the target
      registration contract from the legacy installer's actual limitations.
- [x] Current memory design and implementation plan use the resolved checkout
      contract; historical cutover guidance points to closed tickets.
- [x] Superseded trackers 0978/0986 closed WONTDO; surviving tickets
      0909, 0920, 0923, 0934 and 0988 rebased on this tracker.
- [x] Documentation verification: 112 relevant tests passed; `erg check`
      passed for 511 tickets; `git diff --check` passed.

## Children and review boundaries

- 1003 — runtime registration, installed entry points, guard wiring and safe
  operator documentation in PR #1091. The first independent gate found
  unsafe removal guidance and missed predecessor registration; fixes are
  under re-review. Installation/relocation fixtures preserve independent
  profiles; author live smoke covers Claude/Codex/Pi clean and dirty controls.
- 1002 — dream/provenance helpers and storage-contract defects, extracted to
  handoff-portable-memory for the other memory session. These changes are
  unapproved and not part of #1091. The independent-profile commit failure
  and portable provenance read-count gap remain explicitly open.

The author requested removal of all migration-specific controls: historical
pointer/path-spelling ratchets and old-layout tests are removed from the
registration slice. Current functional installation and guard tests remain.
No real runtime profile is deployed and no memory data is migrated here.

## Remaining work

1. Land reviewed runtime registration through child 1003, retaining precise
   smoke/trust limitations and preserved profile content.
2. Complete child 1002 in the memory session without silently deciding 0988's
   ownership policy. Store reconciliation remains 0934.
3. Review integration across both children before closing this parent.
4. Native packaging, runtime selection/dry-run and opt-in shell/timer setup
   remain follow-on design work, not acceptance claims for child 1003.

## Actions

1. Make every harness-owned entry point derive the checkout from its own real
   location or an explicit root argument; never require `~/.idh` as a pointer.
2. Treat `~/.agents` as the documented default clone and runtime profile paths
   as adapter destinations only.
3. Inventory and remove canonical-path assumptions from code, tests and current
   documentation. Preserve runtime-native paths only where the runtime itself
   owns that path.
4. Define additive, idempotent registration for each supported runtime without
   replacing or owning the runtime's whole profile directory.
5. Verify the same checkout in a second arbitrary absolute location and through
   installed adapter links.

## Test

Run lifecycle, projection, shell-loader and adapter fixtures with a checkout
whose path is neither `~/.agents`, `~/.idh` nor `~/.claude`. Move that fixture
and rerun through the installed links. A hard-coded canonical repository path
must make the test fail.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A fresh clone at `~/.agents` installs supported adapters without a `~/.idh` pointer.
- [ ] The same tests pass from an arbitrary checkout path and after that checkout moves.
- [ ] Runtime profiles remain independently owned and existing unrelated content is preserved.
- [ ] No current code or documentation describes `~/.idh` or `~/.claude` as the repository's canonical location.
- [ ] `make check` passes and live smoke tests cover Claude, Codex and Pi registration.
